{
  "fixture_id": "streams/tool_call_lifecycle",
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "A function_call item arrives complete on response.output_item.done. When a response.output_item.done with item.type=='reasoning' precedes it, that reasoning item is cached against the call_id in an engine-instance-scoped map and replayed verbatim, positioned directly before the function_call item, on the NEXT HTTP request (a separate turn of the tool loop). The cache's bounds and eviction order are asserted here too.",
  "source_tests": [
    "tests/sidecar/ai/engines/test_chatgpt_subscription.py::test_function_call_round_and_follow_up_output_serialization",
    "tests/sidecar/ai/engines/test_chatgpt_subscription.py::test_reasoning_items_are_captured_and_replayed_before_their_function_call"
  ],
  "declarative_verdict": "no",
  "notes": "The second clear carve-out: an opaque provider-issued blob must be cached keyed by call_id, survive across separate HTTP requests within one engine instance, be replayed at an exact list position relative to another item, be deduped by object identity, and be evicted under BOTH a factory-sized count bound and an aggregate byte ceiling. No lookup table expresses 'remember this blob and reinsert it several requests later at a position determined by a DIFFERENT event that has not happened yet'. Note also that the function_call item arrives FULLY FORMED on response.output_item.done: this parser never assembles arguments across response.function_call_arguments.delta events, and whether the real backend ever emits them could not be verified from static analysis alone.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "case_id": "tool_call_then_followup_request",
      "executable": true,
      "binding": "tool_loop_turns",
      "input": {
        "turn_1": {
          "prompt": "Read it",
          "tools": [
            {
              "name": "read_file",
              "description": "Read a file",
              "parameters": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "path": {
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "sse_lines": [
            {
              "type": "response.output_item.done",
              "item": {
                "type": "function_call",
                "name": "read_file",
                "arguments": "{\"path\":\"README.md\"}",
                "call_id": "call_test_1"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "response.completed",
              "response": {
                "usage": {
                  "input_tokens": 5,
                  "output_tokens": 3,
                  "total_tokens": 8
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "turn_2": {
          "messages": [
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "Read it"
            },
            {
              "role": "assistant",
              "content": "",
              "tool_calls": [
                {
                  "name": "read_file",
                  "arguments": {
                    "path": "README.md"
                  },
                  "call_id": "call_test_1"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "tool",
              "tool_call_id": "call_test_1",
              "content": "contents"
            }
          ],
          "sse_lines": [
            {
              "type": "response.output_text.delta",
              "delta": "Done"
            },
            {
              "type": "response.completed",
              "response": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "turn_1_stream_items": [
          {
            "kind": "tool_call",
            "tool_id": "read_file",
            "call_id": "call_test_1",
            "arguments": {
              "path": "README.md"
            },
            "coerced": false
          }
        ],
        "turn_1_result": {
          "content": "",
          "finish_reason": "tool_calls",
          "tool_calls": [
            {
              "tool_id": "read_file",
              "call_id": "call_test_1",
              "arguments": {
                "path": "README.md"
              },
              "coerced": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "turn_1_request_tools": [
          {
            "type": "function",
            "name": "read_file",
            "description": "Read a file",
            "strict": false,
            "parameters": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "path": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "turn_2_request_input_items": [
          {
            "type": "message",
            "role": "user",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "input_text",
                "text": "Read it"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "function_call",
            "name": "read_file",
            "arguments": "{\"path\":\"README.md\"}",
            "call_id": "call_test_1"
          },
          {
            "type": "function_call_output",
            "call_id": "call_test_1",
            "output": "contents"
          }
        ],
        "turn_2_result": {
          "content": "Done",
          "finish_reason": "stop"
        }
      },
      "rule": "A function_call item arrives COMPLETE on response.output_item.done (never assembled from argument-delta events) and finish_reason is overridden to 'tool_calls'. The follow-up request re-serializes the call and its output as a paired function_call/function_call_output couple."
    },
    {
