      "rule": "Eviction is FIFO by FIRST capture, NOT LRU: dict.update() on an existing key does not reorder, so re-capturing c0 keeps its original position and the next insert evicts it. An LRU cache would have evicted c1 instead. Within a tool loop insertion order == call order == replay order, so the two agree in every realistic stream, and FIFO keeps the request-build path read-only and re-entrancy-safe."
